			<div class="content" id="post-content-4474635">
									

<p>okay then, this was a lot to take in. each chapter had a different effect on me, so i'll do a chapter by chapter.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">collapsible&nbsp;just&nbsp;in&nbsp;case</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">7.&nbsp;6.&nbsp;5.&nbsp;4.&nbsp;3.&nbsp;2.&nbsp;1.&nbsp;0.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Chapter 1 &quot;Manor House&quot; / 7:</strong> at first this really confused me until I finished chapter 2, at which point i came back and re-read it. this wasn't precisely the best &quot;hook&quot;, in my opinion, but maybe that's just because i wasn't really invested until 2. the recurring usage of <tt>witness</tt> hinted that something was very off well, thankfully. though, swann preparing it was odd and kinda falsely prepared <em>me</em> for meta. &#8230;at least i think falsely.<br />
<strong>Chapter 2 &quot;You Complete Me&quot; / 6:</strong> this, though, did hook me. the reference to the chains weakening was enough to worry me, honestly. not much else to say here. also thanks talloran, very cool.<br />
<strong>Chapter 3 &quot;When the Man Comes Around&quot; / 5:</strong> later on in the exploration logs, i was fully invested in the logs, picturing it in my head all the while. the church scene was pretty nice. this is also the one that made me realize that the countdown numbers of the chapter were recurring, such as E-5 Pentagon being fives all around the board.<br />
<strong>Chapter 4 &quot;The Exorcism of Savannah Grace&quot; / 4:</strong> the names, while confusing (i think the other works are going to explain those names better), were interesting. as well as the fact that Macneil actually managed to exorcise Grace, considering the fact that Scarlet things were going on. a fun read overall.<br />
<strong>Chapter 5 &quot;Digital Ash in a Digital Urn&quot; / 3:</strong> the most interesting bit of the scip for me, as i was very interested in the effects the game was having on people. the [DATA EXPUNGED]'s felt slightly unsatisfying, though not too much to detract from the chapter overall. RIP <span style="color: blue">Axl</span> (age 9) and thank you smalls (very cool).<br />
<strong>Chapter 6 &quot;Plaything&quot; / 2:</strong> D-002 is cool, and i'm pretty sure Cindy is Cinder. not sure about that. overall a fun chapter, but the final test log suddenly swapping to &quot;the item&quot; without explaining what it was confused me for a moment. the researchers listening to Cindy was also a fun moment, since it showed how easily it could just manipulate them. i don't understand why the final image is spoilered, though. chances are i missed something there.<br />
<strong>Chapter 7 &quot;Scary Stories to Tell in the Dark&quot; / 1:</strong> the point of no return. i think a lot of the clues here fell flat on me, such as the flashlight, marshmallow stick, and <tt>spirals</tt>, but it wasn't bad enough to the point where everything flew over my head. the final location especially was nice. nice chapter title as well. as for &quot;what happened to the bodies&quot;, fuck if i know <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">whitetext</span> glitchtext, i'm as confused as you are!<br />
<strong>The Final Chapter / 0:</strong> admittedly, there's not much to talk about here, but it&#8230; didn't really do much for me? the appearance of the monster - which i assume to be scarlet or one of its pawns? - felt a little fake for me, and the smile at the end just felt off. and the scream felt somewhat cheap? i don't know, it just fell flat on me.<br />
<span style="color: white">you have nothing to lose but your chains, scarlet!</span><br />
+1 over-all, in the end!</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>edit:</strong><br />
fuck yeah, woed! nice css.</p>

